  You are the agent `coder`, working on item #qp7jzs: Dummy: add a hello subcommand note to the README

  ## Task

  Dummy issue to generate a transcript. Read the README, list the crates in the workspace, and summarize them in a
  comment. Make no code changes.

  ## How to work

  - You are in a git worktree on the branch `wf/qp7jzsdzp2cy`, started from `main`. Work only here.
  - Commit small and often: only commits carry over to a later session.
  - Tick each step as soon as it is done, not all at the end: `wf item check qp7jzs <number>`
  - Report while you work: `wf comment qp7jzs "<what you chose, what you rejected, and why>" --step <number>`
    - Add `--done` to tick the step with the same command.
    - Leave out `--step` for a report on the whole item.
    - Write each report so that it makes sense on its own.
  - Need an answer from someone: `wf comment qp7jzs "<question>" --block`, then end your turn. You are prompted again
    once it is answered.
  - Finished: `wf work submit --note "<what the reviewer should know>"`. Your commits are reviewed and merged from
    there.
  - Stuck: `wf work release --note "<why>"`
  - Lost track: `wf work brief` prints this brief again.

␛[1m␛[94mcoder␛[0m  ␛[2m00:49␛[0m
  ␛[32m✓␛[0m ␛[1mBash␛[0m  cat README.md; ls crates; grep -A15 '^\[workspace\]' Cargo.toml; for f in crates/*/  ␛[2mallowed by you␛[0m       ␛[2m0.2s␛[0m
